    "result_text": "All 26 tests pass, including the ones directly covering this change (Cp09, Cp14, Cp16).\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `'<LAST3>-<NNNN>'` to `'<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>'` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n- `nextCustomerCode` now takes both `city` and `lastName`. It builds:\n  - `CITY3` \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the city\n  - `LAST3` \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the last name\n  - `NNNN` \u2014 a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence, computed as one more than the number of owners already in that city (case-insensitive city match), instead of the previous global owner count.\n- The call site in `addOwner` now passes `owner.getCity()`.\n\n**Derived values rebuilt automatically:**\n\n- `membershipNumber` is built by `membershipNumberFor(owner.getCustomerCode(), \u2026)` as `'<customerCode>-M<YY>'`, so it now carries the new city-prefixed code with no further change (verified by Cp14, which recomputes it from returned fields).\n\n`householdId`, `namesakeCount`, and `membershipTier` are derived from other fields (lastName/address, names, email/namesake), not from `customerCode`, so they were correctly left untouched.\n\nThe full suite (26 tests) is green.",
